  "description": "# Conversation Summary\n\n1. **Issue**: The chat history viewer was missing from the application, requiring a way to navigate and view chat details.\n\n2. **Solution**: Created a new `ChatDetailsDrawer.vue` component - a left sidebar drawer that displays comprehensive chat information.\n\n3. **Features**: The drawer includes chat metadata, statistics (message counts, hidden messages, subtasks), timeline history, file management, tags, profiles, and direct navigation to parent/child chats.\n\n4. **Integration**: Updated `ChatView.vue` to integrate the drawer with a toggle button in the header, managing the drawer's open/close state.\n\n5. **Result**: Users now have a dedicated left panel to explore chat hierarchy, view chat details, manage context files, and perform quick actions like creating subtasks or accessing settings.",
